cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Citation Integrity in Frontier Language Models: Author Misattribution and Fabrication in Research-Agent Conditions"
abstract: >
  We evaluate the citation accuracy of three frontier language models—DeepSeek,
  Claude, and ChatGPT—when forced to provide formal academic references in
  response to research questions. Across 15 responses and 45 citations spanning
  three domains, we find that 71% of citations were real and accurate, 27% were
  real but distorted (primarily author misattribution), and 2% were fully
  fabricated. The dominant failure mode is not fabrication of non-existent
  papers but distortion of existing papers, most commonly by attributing them
  to incorrect authors.
